@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About | LMS HA Edge Gateway</PageTitle>

<div class="page-shell edge-gateway-page lms-about-page">
    <section class="surface-card edge-card lms-about-hero">
        <div class="lms-about-hero-copy">
            <img class="lms-about-logo" src="images/lms-edge-gateway-icon.png" alt="" />
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">LMS HA Edge Gateway</p>
                <h2>Secure Home Assistant publishing powered by Linux Made Sane</h2>
                <p class="meta-text">
                    LMS HA Edge Gateway is the Home Assistant add-on edition of the Linux Made Sane Edge Gateway. It brings
                    the LMS control-plane approach to Cloudflare Tunnel, Caddy routing, MFA, passkeys, and safe publishing
                    of Home Assistant-adjacent services.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <img class="lms-about-splash" src="images/lms-ha-login-art.png" alt="LMS Edge Gateway for Home Assistant artwork." />
    </section>

    <section class="surface-card edge-card lms-about-section">
        <div class="table-header">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
                <h2>Expose internal services without hand-building the edge stack</h2>
                <p class="meta-text">
                    The add-on manages the public Cloudflare edge, the local tunnel connector, and the Caddy routes that
                    forward traffic to the right service on your Home Assistant network.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lms-about-feature-list">
            <article>
                <strong>Cloudflare relay</strong>
                <span>Creates or reuses a Cloudflare Tunnel, maintains DNS records, and keeps tunnel ingress aligned with the routes you publish.</span>
            </article>
            <article>
                <strong>Local Caddy routing</strong>
                <span>Routes each public hostname to the correct internal target, with route-specific headers, path handling, and upstream TLS settings.</span>
            </article>
            <article>
                <strong>LMS authentication</strong>
                <span>Protects browser-first services with LMS MFA, passkeys, email OTP, source rules, and explicit pass-through modes for apps with their own auth.</span>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="surface-card edge-card lms-about-section">
        <div class="table-header">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Base project</p>
                <h2>Built from the Linux Made Sane platform</h2>
                <p class="meta-text">
                    Linux Made Sane is the parent project behind the shared UI language, service orchestration patterns,
                    authentication experience, and local-first operations model used by this Home Assistant add-on.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lms-about-media-grid">
            <figure class="lms-about-figure">
                <img src="images/lms-edge-gateway-icon.png" alt="LMS Edge Gateway icon." />
                <figcaption>LMS HA Edge Gateway packages the LMS edge workflow as a Home Assistant add-on.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <div class="lms-about-facts">
                <div>
                    <strong>Shared foundation</strong>
                    <span>Uses LMS-style navigation, status surfaces, setup flows, diagnostics, and operational guardrails.</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Home Assistant edition</strong>
                    <span>Runs inside the Home Assistant add-on lifecycle with ingress UI, persistent <code>/data</code>, and supervised services.</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Security boundary</strong>
                    <span>Combines LMS authentication policies with app-aware pass-through for clients that need their own native login flow.</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Route ownership</strong>
                    <span>Cloudflare handles the public edge and tunnel transport; Caddy handles local routing and policy enforcement.</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="surface-card edge-card lms-about-section">
        <div class="table-header">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Links</p>
                <h2>Project references</h2>
                <p class="meta-text">LMS HA Edge Gateway is part of the Linux Made Sane ecosystem and is published as a dedicated Home Assistant add-on repository.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lms-about-links">
            <a class="lms-button lms-button-primary" href="https://www.linuxmadesane.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Linux Made Sane</a>
            <a class="lms-button" href="https://github.com/lmsowner/ha_addon_lms_edge_gateway" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">HA add-on repo</a>
            <a class="lms-button" href="https://github.com/lmsowner/linuxmadesanerelease" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Base LMS repo</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
